<p>NASA&#x27;s four-person Artemis II crew spent Tuesday heading back toward Earth after a crewed lunar flyby, sharing a widely circulated &quot;Earthset&quot; image that shows Earth dipping below the Moon&#x27;s horizon and speaking publicly about what they saw during the mission. The crew — Reid Wiseman, Christina Koch, Victor Glover and Canadian astronaut Jeremy Hansen — also held what reports described as the first ship-to-ship space call with astronauts aboard the International Space Station, creating a live exchange between crews in deep space and low Earth orbit. The mission reached several milestones highlighted across the reports: Artemis II carried humans around the Moon for the first time since the Apollo era, traveled beyond Apollo 13&#x27;s distance record from Earth, and serves as a key step in NASA&#x27;s broader effort to return astronauts to the lunar surface in 2028. Along the way, the astronauts described flashes on the lunar surface consistent with meteoroid impacts, unusual color variations, levitated dust, and a total solar eclipse seen from lunar orbit, giving scientists and the public a vivid new look at the Moon as the crew prepares for splashdown in the Pacific off California late Friday.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MoBCZGpiwpnuhmCNd8pnHk_ofIYD2Zj-oEr7Y-_aVY3SrGOlUyanF6xS1LcDtlawNOCRROyEnC6FxY8fj81dD0NRnYohFXsW-DqpMJo_piWW' alt='This handout picture released on April 7 by Nasa shows Earth as it dips beyond the lunar horizon, also known as an ‘Earthset’, as seen from the Orion spacecraft on April 6.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>A new vantage: AllSides said the route gave the crew views of parts of the Moon that no human had ever seen before.</li><li>Lighting effects: Mercopress highlighted the crew&#x27;s description that &quot;the Moon became a sponge of light,&quot; capturing how dramatically changing illumination shaped their view during the flyby.</li><li>Binational profile: Straits Times said the U.S.-Canadian makeup of the crew gave the mission a broader international profile.</li><li>Political outreach: Dawn reported that NASA Administrator Jared Isaacman and President Trump called the crew to congratulate them after the lunar flyby.</li></ul><blockquote>Humans probably have not evolved to see what we’re seeing. It is truly hard to describe. It is amazing. - Victor Glover</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>NASA science team: The post-flyby exchange served as a rapid science debrief, with NASA gathering first-person descriptions while the crew was still making its way back to Earth. (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/07/the-moon-became-a-sponge-of-light-artemis-ii-astronauts-share-their-observations'>MercoPress</a>)</li><li>White House: The White House amplified the mission imagery by recirculating the far-side Moon photo and presenting it as a notable first from the voyage. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1989536/artemis-ii-crew-snaps-historic-earthset-photo-on-way-home'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>International media: Straits Times framed the flight as a welcome break from a news cycle dominated by conflict, tariffs, and fraying institutions, rather than focusing mainly on technical milestones. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-and-canadian-astronauts-capture-global-attention-with-artemis-ii-moon-flight'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/science/article/2026/04/07/artemis-ii-astronauts-head-towards-earth-sharing-lunar-flyby-moments_6752198_10.html'>Artemis II astronauts head toward Earth, sharing lunar flyby moments</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/us-and-canadian-astronauts-capture-global-attention-with-artemis-ii-moon-flight'>US and Canadian astronauts capture global attention with Artemis II moon flight</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/united-states-canada/article/3349308/nasas-artemis-crew-snaps-historic-earthset-photo-way-home-moon'>Artemis crew snap historic Earthset photo and call space station on way home</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/artemis-ii-moon-mission-moon-crew-iss-astronauts-speak-on-first-ship-to-ship-space-call-11326670#publisher=newsstand'>Artemis II Crew, ISS Astronauts Speak On First Ship-To-Ship Space Call</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/04/07/the-moon-became-a-sponge-of-light-artemis-ii-astronauts-share-their-observations'>“The Moon became a sponge of light”: Artemis II astronauts share their observations</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/artemis-ii-crew-snaps-earthset-in-throwback-to-apollo-8/a-76698514'>Artemis II: Crew snaps &#x27;Earthset&#x27; in throwback to Apollo 8</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-07-0700/science-artemis-ii-crew-saw-parts-moon-never-seen-heres-what-they-said'>The Artemis II crew saw parts of the moon never seen before. Here&#x27;s what they said</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1989536/artemis-ii-crew-snaps-historic-earthset-photo-on-way-home'>Artemis II crew snaps historic ‘Earthset’ photo on way home</a> - dawn.com</li></ul>